{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\n`gh project item-list` asks for something like `fieldValues(first: 100)` per item, so its cost scales with the requested limit (measured: `--limit 500` ≈ 101 points, `--limit 100` still tens). #163 shrank the limits, but the structural waste — fetching every field value of every item — remains.\n\n## Spec\n\n- Replace both calls with `gh api graphql` queries that fetch only what the page renders: `items(first: N)` sized to the known `totalCount`, and `fieldValues(first: K)` limited to the fields in use (`Status` plus whatever the current view references for columns, grouping, sorting and dates). `fields(first: 30)` returns only name / type / options.\n- Convert the response into the existing `ProjectItem` / `ProjectField` shapes (the `gh` JSON layout) so the panes stay untouched; redacted items (`content: null`) keep working; user and organization projects both supported.\n- Piggy-back `rateLimit { cost remaining }` on the query, measure the real cost of a board fetch and feed the figure into the status bar's remaining-points display. Target: **≤ 10 points per board fetch** (from ~50).\n\n## Tests\n\nResponse → type conversion against fixtures, the generated query's field narrowing, and the measured cost recorded in the PR.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-08T08:11:43Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":169,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Projects: replace item-list / field-list with a hand-written GraphQL query (~1/5 the cost)"}
